.TH IMUD\-CAL 8 "2026-07-11" "imud 1.4" "System Manager's Manual"
.SH NAME
imud\-cal \- IMU calibration tool for imud
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B imud-cal
[\fB\-\-config\fR \fIPATH\fR]
[\fB\-\-output\fR \fIPATH\fR]
.I mode
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B imud-cal
performs interactive sensor calibration and writes the result to a JSON
calibration file read by
.BR imud (8)
at startup.
.PP
Each mode operates the hardware directly (without the daemon running) and
guides the operator through a collection procedure via stdout prompts.
Results are merged into the calibration file: existing sections for other
modes are preserved.
.PP
Run
.B imud-cal
once after installing the hardware.
Re-run after physically repositioning the sensor or after a hard reset
that clears non-volatile sensor registers.
.SH MODES
.TP
.B gyro
Gyroscope bias capture.
Keep the board completely still during collection.
The bias vector is averaged over the settle window and written to the
calibration file.
Takes approximately 5\(en10 seconds.
.TP
.B accel
Accelerometer 6-position calibration.
Place the board in each of the six cardinal orientations
(+X, \-X, +Y, \-Y, +Z, \-Z face up) as prompted.
Fits a scale-and-offset model that corrects for sensitivity and misalignment.
Takes approximately 2\(en5 minutes.
.TP
.B mag
Magnetometer hard/soft-iron calibration.
Perform at least two slow 360\(de rotations about each axis in the local
magnetic environment (away from large metal objects).
Fits an ellipsoid model that corrects for hard-iron offsets and soft-iron
distortion.
Takes approximately 3\(en10 minutes.
.IP
The collection is guided: a live bar shows the heading circle split into
24 sectors (\(oq#\(cq covered, \(oq.\(cq still needed, \(oqo\(cq the
direction currently pointed), with a running coverage percentage and, once
enough samples exist, the live field radius and RMS fit residual. When
every sector is covered the tool sounds a bell and says so \(em one more
circle then improves the fit; press Ctrl-C to finish.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-\-config \ PATH
Config file to use.
Defaults to
.I /etc/imud/imud.conf
(then
.IR ~/.config/imud/imud.conf ).
Determines which sensor driver, I2C bus, and GPIO lines to use.
.TP
.BI \-\-output \ PATH
Write calibration output to
.I PATH
instead of the path set by
.B calibration.file
in the config.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /etc/imud/cal.json
Default calibration output path.
.TP
.I /etc/imud/imud.conf
Default configuration file.
.SH NOTES
The daemon
.RB ( imud )
and
.B imud-cal
must not run simultaneously; both open the same I2C device.
Stop the daemon before running calibration:
.PP
.RS 4
.EX
sudo systemctl stop imud
sudo imud-cal --config /etc/imud/imud.conf mag
sudo systemctl start imud
.EE
.RE
.SH EXIT STATUS
.B 0
on success,
.B 1
on configuration or hardware error.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR imud (8),
.BR imud.conf (5)
.SH AUTHORS
Richard Simpson
